(footprint "INMP441_Module_2x3_P2.54mm"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "vibecoder-handbuilt")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "INMP441 I2S MEMS microphone module, round 14.0 mm board, SOCKETED: two 1x3 female headers are soldered into these six holes and the module's own male pins plug into them, so the module is removable. It is still ONE KiCad component, not a pair of separate socket parts - the six holes belong to this footprint. Geometry measured with FreeCAD from the module STEP: six 0.635 mm square posts on a 2.54 mm pitch, the two rows 7.62 mm apart (0.3 inch - the seller's hand-measured '7 mm' was approximate), board outline a true circle (measured perimeter 43.975 vs pi*14 = 43.982) centred exactly on the pin grid, and a 0.9 mm acoustic port dead centre of that circle. Assembly height: official PinSocket_1x03_P2.54mm_Vertical body is 8.50 mm tall, the module's header plastic lands on the socket's top face, and the module itself is 5.08 mm tall (header plastic 2.54 + module PCB 1.26 + pin stub 1.28), so the whole stack is 13.58 mm above the board and the acoustic port sits at 12.30 mm. The module's pins are 6.35 mm long and insert into an 8.50 mm deep socket. A low-profile socket would cut this down; if one is used, re-measure and update the 3D offset (module model offset.z = socket top height - 7.0). Pads are NAMED for their signals rather than numbered, because this module has no printed pin numbers - only silkscreen labels - and numbering it invents an authority that does not exist on the part. Layout matches the maker photo as seen from the KiCad TOP view: upper row L/R WS SCK left to right, lower row SD VDD GND left to right. That is not a coincidence to be reproduced by luck - the module is fitted label-side-out, so the top view is NOT mirrored, and drawing the footprint the same way round as the photo is the cheapest defence against a mirror error. Components and the mic itself sit on the UNDERSIDE of the module PCB; sound enters through the centre port on the TOP face, so the enclosure acoustic stack must aim at the module's top centre.")
	(tags "INMP441 I2S MEMS microphone module 14mm round 2x3 header")
